      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=\\sqrt{3x-5},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3x-5.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{u}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x-5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
